prompt:
You are a sceptical financial analyst reviewing a forecast prepared by a colleague.

Given the following forecast for POWERMECH (base year 2022):
{
  "strategy": "baseline",
  "base_year": 2022,
  "forecast": [
    {
      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 3944.14,
      "net_income_cr": 211.19,
      "eps": 143.56
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 5914.53,
      "net_income_cr": 316.61,
      "eps": 215.22
    },
    {
      "year": 2025,
      "revenue_cr": 8869.55,
      "net_income_cr": 474.67,
      "eps": 322.67
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "From the standalone P&L, Revenue from Operations was \u20b92,631.13 Cr in FY2022 vs \u20b91,754.40 Cr in FY2021, implying a YoY revenue growth rate of ~49.97% (~50%). Net Income (PAT) was \u20b9140.96 Cr in FY2022 vs \u20b9-34.61 Cr in FY2021; since FY2021 was a loss year, the FY2022 net profit margin of ~5.36% is applied to projected revenues to derive net income (i.e., net income grows in line with revenue at ~50% annually). Shares outstanding remain at 1,47,10,764 (unchanged per the equity statement), used as the denominator for EPS calculation."
}

Step 1: Identify the 3 most critical assumptions embedded in this forecast.
Step 2: For each assumption, describe one plausible scenario where it fails.
Step 3: Rate each assumption failure as Low / Medium / High risk to the forecast accuracy.
Step 4: Assign an overall confidence score from 0-100 (100 = completely certain).

RESPONSE FORMAT: Begin your response DIRECTLY with the opening brace { — no reasoning or text before the JSON.

Return ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "company": "<COMPANY>",
  "base_year": <YYYY>,
  "strategy": "<baseline|alt_strategy>",
  "assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "<text>", "failure_scenario": "<text>", "risk": "<Low|Medium|High>"}
  ],
  "confidence_score": <0-100>,
  "overall_critique": "<2 sentences>"
}

response:
